 "equipment_type": "Unit ventilator controller (fan coil / terminal unit)",
 "applies_to": "Carrier unit ventilators with the factory-installed Unit Vent (OPN-UV) multi-protocol controller.",
 "summary": "The Unit Vent (OPN-UV) is Carrier's i-Vu Open controller for unit ventilators. DIP switches select BACnet MS/TP (the default), BACnet ARC156, Modbus or N2, and a LonWorks option card is available. The points list has about 70 objects: setpoints, space, supply and outdoor temperatures, valve and damper outputs, enables, alarms and the 'system' points a BAS writes in place of local sensors.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet ARC156"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "16101xx (xx = rotary switch address)",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "System points (system_spt, system_iaq, system_oat, system_stpt_adj, system_water_temp) must be written at BACnet priority 16 and no more than once a minute; -999 means no network value.",
  "The guide's general system-point table also lists system_rh (AV:1904), system_oaq (AV:1908), oae (BV:1901), press_override (BV:1906) and fire_shutdown (BV:1907). They are not in the Unit Vent points list, so they are left out here.",
  "Four rows are printed with the display name 'Setpoint'; the descriptions here say which setpoint each object name is.",
  "System Mode (run_status) prints state 12 twice (IAQ Override and Pre-occ Purge); kept as printed.",
  "Defaults in the points list differ from the sequence text for the fan delays (Fan Off Delay 90 s vs 120 s, Fan On Delay 10 s vs 30 s); check on the controller.",
  "Each point also has a Modbus register in the same table (some later rows have none); only the BACnet side is captured here."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Unit Ventilator Integration Guide (Appendix A: Unit Vent Network Points List)",
  "doc_number": "11-808-513-01",
  "revision_date": "2022-08-02",
  "url": "https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1000/Public/0D/11-808-513-01.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Set the Unit Vent for BACnet MS/TP with its DIP switches and rotary address. Disable the local Occupancy Schedules so the BAS can command occupancy through keypad_ovrde, then write setpoints directly. Space temperature, CO2, OAT and changeover water temperature from the BMS go into the system_* points at priority 16 and have to be refreshed within each point's window.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "MV 1001",
    "name": "keypad_ovrde",
    "why": "BAS occupancy command: occupied/unoccupied"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 9001",
    "name": "shutdown",
    "why": "Network shutdown command"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3001",
    "name": "occ_cl_stpt",
    "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3002",
    "name": "occ_ht_stpt",
    "why": "Occupied heating setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 2002",
    "name": "run_status",
    "why": "Current system mode"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 2008",
    "name": "occ_status",
    "why": "Confirms occupied/unoccupied"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 2007",
    "name": "space_temp",
    "why": "Space temperature the unit controls to"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1008",
    "name": "sa_temp",
    "why": "Supply air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 7008",
    "name": "sfan_fail_alarm",
    "why": "Supply fan failure alarm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 7037",
    "name": "llt_alarm",
    "why": "Freezestat (low limit) alarm"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "The unit runs occupied 24/7 until a schedule or the BAS takes over. Disable Occupancy Schedules (Configuration > Unit Configuration) so the BAS can control it, then write BAS On/Off keypad_ovrde (MSV:1001): 1=Inactive, 2=Occupied, 3=Unoccupied. The system-point table says the occupancy control configuration must be set to 3 (BAS On/Off). Shutdown (BV:9001) stops the unit; Cool Enable (BV:1011) and Heat Enable (BV:1012) lock out cooling or heating.",
  "heartbeat": "No general heartbeat. Each system point is only used while it is refreshed within its window: space temperature 1 min / 5 min, CO2 5 min / 10 min, OAT and water temperature 5 min / 60 min.",
  "remote_sensors": "Write system_spt (AV:1902), system_iaq (AV:1903), system_oat (AV:1901), system_water_temp (AV:1905) and system_stpt_adj (AV:1913) at BACnet priority 16, no more than once a minute. The controller clears a system point after processing it, so read the matching control point instead (space_temp, iaq, oa_temp, chgovr_mode) at least 30 s after the write.",
  "setup": [
   "MS/TP MAC address is set on the Tens and Ones rotary switches (1-99); read only at power-up.",
   "Device instance defaults to 16101xx (xx = rotary address); it can be changed with an Equipment Touch.",
   "Baud on DIP switches 1-2 (9600/19.2k/38.4k/76.8k, 76.8k default); DIP 3 and 4 both Off for BACnet MS/TP; 8N1.",
   "Max Masters defaults to 127 and Max Info Frames to 10 (Equipment Touch). The controller counts as a full load on the MS/TP bus."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "System points must be written at priority 16; writes at any other priority are ignored.",
   "Never write a system point more than once per minute.",
   "Only controllers set as MS/TP masters answer Who-Is.",
   "Demand level points (cool_demand_level, heat_demand_level) are read-only in this list, although the guide says the unit accepts three demand levels from the network."
  ]
 },
